@startuml blackboard

' ============================================================
' VISUAL THEME
' ============================================================

left to right direction
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam roundcorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #57606A
skinparam DefaultFontName "SansSerif"
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF

skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam packageBackgroundColor #F6F8FA
skinparam packageBorderColor #57606A

skinparam classBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam classBorderColor #57606A
skinparam classFontColor #24292F

skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFF8C5
skinparam noteBorderColor #57606A

frame "CD - Definition Blackboard Manager - Server-side data model" {

  ' ============================================================
  ' DBM NOTE
  ' ============================================================

  note as DbmNote
    **DBM -- Definition Blackboard Manager (Server-side data model)**

    Generic, domain-agnostic blackboard substrate. The single top-level
    resource is `Blackboard`. The service is a **passive store of facts**:
    it persists client-posted contributions, validates them per-slot, and
    seals the contribution set. It does NOT reduce contributions.

    Reduction is **controller-side** -- a client-owned process over the
    byte-stable sealed contribution stream. See SKILL.md section 5.

    All entities below are persisted server-side and exposed as REST
    sub-resources of `Blackboard`. Client sourcers declare their domain
    ontology entirely as data: panels and slot schemas. The service
    holds no hardcoded domain concept, no resolver, no merge logic.

    **Minimality**: this model is intentionally minimal; it will be
    enriched only when concrete needs surface on the ITIP client side.

    Lifecycle invariants enforced server-side:
    - Panel topology is **frozen** when the first contribution is
      accepted on the Blackboard.
    - A Blackboard transitions through `OPEN -> SEALING -> SEALED`
      exactly once; no further writes accepted after `SEALED`.
    - The sealed contribution stream is **byte-stable**; this is the
      audit anchor that client-side reducers replay against.
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' BLACKBOARD
  ' ============================================================

  class Blackboard {
    +getId(): URI
    +getName(): String
    +getTimestamp(): Instant
    +getStatus(): BlackboardStatus
    +getSealTimestamp(): Instant?
    +getPanels(): Panel[]
  }

  note bottom of Blackboard
    **Blackboard** -- top-level resource of the substrate.

    **Concept Semantics**:

    - A Blackboard is a self-standing, client-instantiated workspace into
      which Knowledge Sources (client-side) post Contributions over REST.
    - **Isolation**: each Blackboard is a fully isolated unit of work.
      The service performs no cross-Blackboard sequencing, chaining, or
      coupling, and exposes no inter-Blackboard relation. Any client
      flow that happens to span multiple Blackboards is responsible for
      its own bookkeeping out-of-band; the substrate has no knowledge
      of it.
    - The Blackboard owns its lifecycle: `OPEN -> SEALING -> SEALED`
      (success) or `OPEN | SEALING -> ABORTED` (client abort or
      irrecoverable failure). SEALED is terminal; the contribution
      stream becomes byte-stable and the audit ledger is closed.

    **Attribute Semantics**:

    - `id`: server-minted resource identifier (URI). Immutable.
    - `name`: client-supplied free-form label; not interpreted by the
      service.
    - `timestamp`: creation timestamp.
    - `status`: lifecycle state (BlackboardStatus).
    - `sealTimestamp`: set on transition to `SEALED`; null otherwise.
    - `panels`: the panel set declared on this Blackboard.

    **Validation Rules**:

    - `id` MUST NOT be null.
    - `name` is free-form; uniqueness is per server-minted `id`.
    - `status` transitions MUST follow the FSM (see `blackboard-lifecycle.puml`).
    - Once `status = SEALED`, no further Contributions or Panels may be
      written; the Blackboard is immutable except for audit-ledger reads.

    **Assignment Rules**:

    - `id`, `timestamp` are assigned at create time and
      MUST NOT be modified.
    - `name` comes from the create-call body and MUST NOT be modified
      after creation.
    - `sealTimestamp` is assigned by the seal transition.
  end note

  enum BlackboardStatus {
    OPEN
    SEALING
    SEALED
    ABORTED
  }

  note bottom of BlackboardStatus
    **BlackboardStatus** -- Blackboard lifecycle (sealed enum).

    **Concept Semantics**:

    - `OPEN`: writes accepted; reads return the live contribution view.
    - `SEALING`: transient state during the seal transition; writes
      are rejected (409) and the contribution stream is being frozen.
    - `SEALED`: terminal-success; contribution stream is byte-stable
      and the audit ledger is closed. Reads remain available.
    - `ABORTED`: terminal-failure; reached from `OPEN` (client abort) or
      `SEALING` (irrecoverable failure). Writes rejected (409).

    See `blackboard-lifecycle.puml` for the authoritative FSM.
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' PANEL
  ' ============================================================

  class Panel {
    +getId(): URI
    +getBlackboard(): Blackboard
    +getName(): String
    +getDescription(): String
    +getSlots(): ContributionSlot[]
  }

  note bottom of Panel
    **Panel** -- client-declared topological unit grouping ContributionSlots.

    **Concept Semantics**:

    - A Panel is a client-namespaced grouping of ContributionSlots inside
      a Blackboard. The service does not interpret panel semantics; it
      only enforces structural invariants (namespacing, freezing).
    - Panel topology is **frozen** as soon as the first Contribution is
      accepted on the Blackboard.

    **Attribute Semantics**:

    - `id`: server-minted resource identifier (URI). Immutable.
    - `blackboard`: parent Blackboard (composition back-reference).
    - `name`: client-namespaced (`{clientPrefix}:{LocalName}`).
    - `description`: free-form documentation. Mandatory.
    - `slots`: the ContributionSlots declared on this panel.

    **Validation Rules**:

    - `name` MUST be client-namespaced; reserved prefixes `bb:` and
      `_internal:` are rejected.
    - `description` MUST be non-empty.
    - Once any Contribution is accepted on the Blackboard, the panel
      topology is frozen (no add/remove/edit of panels or slots).

    **Assignment Rules**:

    - `id` is server-minted at registration and MUST NOT be modified.
    - `blackboard`, `name`, `description` assigned at registration and
      MUST NOT be modified.
  end note

  class ContributionSlot {
    +getId(): URI
    +getPanel(): Panel
    +getName(): String
    +getSchemaUri(): URI
    +getContributions(): Contribution[]
  }

  note bottom of ContributionSlot
    **ContributionSlot** -- typed write surface inside a Panel.

    **Concept Semantics**:

    - A ContributionSlot is the typed surface against which Contributions
      are validated. It carries the slot's JSON Schema URI.
    - Multiple Contributions per slot are accepted; reducing them is a
      client-controller concern over the sealed stream (see SKILL.md
      section 5).

    **Attribute Semantics**:

    - `id`: server-minted resource identifier (URI). Immutable.
    - `panel`: parent Panel (composition back-reference).
    - `name`: slot name, unique within its parent Panel.
    - `schemaUri`: JSON Schema URI for `Contribution.post`; MUST be
      retrievable by the service (cached by URI).
    - `contributions`: the Contributions accepted into this slot.

    **Validation Rules**:

    - `name` MUST be unique within its Panel.
    - `schemaUri` MUST be retrievable; resolution failure rejects the
      panel registration.

    **Assignment Rules**:

    - `id` is server-minted at panel registration and MUST NOT be
      modified.
    - `panel`, `name`, `schemaUri` are assigned at panel registration
      and frozen with the panel.
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' CONTRIBUTION
  ' ============================================================

  class Contribution {
    +getId(): URI
    +getContributionSlot(): ContributionSlot
    +getPost(): JsonObject
    +getDerivedContribution(): Contribution[]
    +getTimestamp(): Instant
  }

  note bottom of Contribution
    **Contribution** -- single fact posted by a client KS or reducer.

    **Concept Semantics**:

    - A Contribution is an immutable, server-validated fact recorded
      against a `ContributionSlot` of an `OPEN` Blackboard. Once
      persisted it never changes; it appears in the byte-stable sealed
      stream after seal.
    - Contributions are written by client-side producers (Knowledge
      Sources or client reducers/controllers). The substrate does not
      distinguish them.

    **Attribute Semantics**:

    - `id`: server-minted contribution URI; appears in the sealed stream.
    - `contributionSlot`: parent ContributionSlot (composition back-reference).
    - `post`: validated against `slot.schemaUri` at POST time.
    - `derivedContribution`: optional in-Blackboard contribution lineage;
      MUST reference contributions in the **same** Blackboard
      (Blackboards are isolated; no cross-Bb references).
    - `timestamp`: server-assigned timestamp; participates in the
      sealed-stream ordering.

    **Validation Rules**:

    - Blackboard MUST be `OPEN`; POST against `SEALING` or `SEALED`
      returns 409.
    - `post` MUST validate against `slot.schemaUri`; failure returns
      422 (no record persisted).
    - `derivedContribution` URIs MUST reference contributions in the
      **same** Blackboard; cross-Blackboard URIs are rejected (422).

    **Assignment Rules**:

    - All fields are assigned at POST time and MUST NOT be modified.
  end note

  ' ============================================================
  ' RELATIONSHIPS
  ' ============================================================

  Blackboard --> BlackboardStatus
  Blackboard "1" *-- "1..*" Panel
  Panel "1" *-- "1..*" ContributionSlot
  ContributionSlot "1" *-- "0..*" Contribution
  Contribution "0..*" --> "0..*" Contribution : derivedContribution
}

@enduml
